================================================================================
Data provenance and non-commercial / educational use
================================================================================

This project is a non-commercial, educational research tool. It fetches data
from third-party sources and publishes only DERIVED, non-substitutive outputs
(computed facts, ratings, slopes, indexed returns — never raw upstream payloads)
to the public `data` branch, consistent with the redistribution analysis in
docs/data-sources.md.

This project is NOT affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any data
provider below. Trademarks (e.g. "S&P 500®" / S&P Dow Jones Indices,
"CNN Fear & Greed Index", "SPDR®") belong to their respective owners. Nothing
here is investment advice.

- Yahoo Finance (via the `yfinance` library) — equity/ETF/index quotes and
  fundamentals. https://legal.yahoo.com/us/en/yahoo/terms/otos/index.html
  Only derived state (resolution booleans, slopes, indexed returns) is persisted;
  raw `.info`/`.fast_info`/price payloads are never committed.
- CNN Fear & Greed Index — numeric headline scores only.
  https://www.cnn.com/terms
- CBOE Interest Rate Indices `^TNX` / `^FVX` (via Yahoo) — only the derived
  5s10s slope (10y − 5y) is persisted, not raw index levels.
- SPDR S&P 500 ETF (`SPY`, State Street; via Yahoo) — only a derived indexed
  return (rebased to 100) is persisted, never raw closing prices and never the
  S&P 500 index level. The S&P 500® index is the intellectual property of S&P
  Dow Jones Indices LLC and is not reproduced here. See docs/decisions/0011.
- SEC EDGAR — U.S. federal public-domain data (17 U.S.C. § 105).
- usaspending.gov — U.S. federal public-domain data (DATA Act, 31 U.S.C. § 6101).

